WEBVTT

00:01.318 --> 00:04.652
        ♪<i> It seems today</i>
      <i> that all you see</i> ♪

00:04.672 --> 00:08.248
    ♪<i> Is violence in movies</i>
       <i> and sex on TV</i> ♪

00:08.342 --> 00:11.752
     ♪<i> But where are those</i>
 <i> good old-fashioned values</i> ♪

00:11.904 --> 00:14.013
 ♪<i> On which we used to rely?</i> ♪

00:14.164 --> 00:17.665
 ♪<i> Lucky there's a family guy</i> ♪

00:17.760 --> 00:21.336
   ♪<i> Lucky there's a man who</i>
     <i> positively can do</i> ♪

00:21.355 --> 00:22.837
♪<i> All the things that make us</i> ♪

00:22.857 --> 00:24.097
       ♪<i> Laugh and cry</i> ♪

00:24.174 --> 00:30.029
         ♪<i> He's... a...</i>
     <i> Fam... ily... Guy.</i> ♪

00:33.442 --> 00:35.534
         Sorry I'm late.
     Had a family emergency

00:35.685 --> 00:38.779
   with, um... I don't know.
     I want to say Chris?

00:38.873 --> 00:40.447
     Uh, I wasn't listening
          super close.

00:40.599 --> 00:42.599
     Why don't you sit down
         and drink beer

00:42.618 --> 00:45.527
and tell us about it instead of
 being home with your family?

00:45.546 --> 00:47.454
   Apparently, Chris and his
     girlfriend broke up.

00:47.606 --> 00:49.956
  Something about her wanting
     to see other people.

00:50.051 --> 00:52.609
      So the doctor says
     this surgery is gonna

00:52.611 --> 00:53.794
      restore my eyesight.

00:53.962 --> 00:55.703
         What? Oh, no.

00:55.723 --> 00:56.871
           "Oh, no"?

00:56.965 --> 00:59.541
 But I thought you'd be happy,
        Colin Farrell.

00:59.635 --> 01:02.043
  Oi, blimey. Uh, get stuffed.

01:02.063 --> 01:04.121
 I'm-I'm gonna see other birds.

01:04.123 --> 01:06.473
       G-Good day, mate.

01:06.625 --> 01:10.402
    Don't look. Don't look.
 I think that's Colin Farrell.

01:10.554 --> 01:12.629
          And this girl
       was his first love.

01:12.648 --> 01:14.907
          Poor Chris.
  He was sobbing his eyes out

01:15.058 --> 01:16.224
     when I abruptly left.

01:16.393 --> 01:18.560
       First loves always
        hit the hardest.

01:18.654 --> 01:21.805
   I'll say. I still remember
       my first real love.

01:21.824 --> 01:23.082
     Seems like yesterday.

01:23.309 --> 01:24.975
 Why, just thinking back on her
        makes everything

01:24.993 --> 01:27.477
  all shimmery and distorted.

01:27.496 --> 01:29.313
         <i> I was working</i>
     <i> for Federal Express,</i>

01:29.406 --> 01:31.090
 <i> like Tom Hanks in</i> Cast Away.

01:31.317 --> 01:33.166
   <i> And just like Tom Hanks</i>
        <i> in</i> Cast Away,

01:33.319 --> 01:35.168
      <i> I said the words</i>
      <i> "Federal Express"</i>

01:35.321 --> 01:36.653
<i> a suspicious number of times.</i>

01:36.822 --> 01:39.656
     Excuse me, miss. Asking
 as a Federal Express employee,

01:39.675 --> 01:42.542
   may I please get a refill
   of iced tea very quickly,

01:42.603 --> 01:44.995
    the way Federal Express
       delivers parcels?

01:45.013 --> 01:47.164
   <i> There was only one thing</i>
         <i> I loved more</i>

01:47.182 --> 01:48.774
<i>than corporate-branded content,</i>

01:49.001 --> 01:51.276
   <i> and that was my fiancée,</i>
          <i> Helen Hunt.</i>

01:51.503 --> 01:52.444
      <i> JOE: Hubba-hubba.</i>

01:52.596 --> 01:54.004
          <i> QUAGMIRE:</i>
   <i> Darn right hubba-hubba.</i>

01:54.097 --> 01:55.856
    <i> You know how most guys</i>
    <i> want their girlfriends</i>

01:56.008 --> 01:57.357
  <i> to look like a pissy bird?</i>

01:57.509 --> 01:59.601
<i> Well, I was living the dream.</i>

01:59.620 --> 02:01.027
    You're 17 seconds late.

02:01.180 --> 02:02.979
I am a Federal Express employee

02:02.981 --> 02:04.623
who is very obsessed with time.

02:04.700 --> 02:06.366
    Well, that's my fiancé.

02:06.518 --> 02:09.035
      Give me a kiss, you
  time-obsessed beardless man

02:09.188 --> 02:11.521
     who is unable to spear
 a fish with a sharpened stick.

02:11.540 --> 02:13.114
     <i> QUAGMIRE: Remember</i>
  <i> all that stuff for later.</i>

02:13.208 --> 02:16.135
     Mm, oh, I can't wait
     to do more than kiss.

02:16.286 --> 02:17.861
      Only three more days
        till the wedding.

02:18.030 --> 02:20.455
       Yep. I've got just
         one last flight

02:20.474 --> 02:23.175
   across the Planecrash Sea,
     and then I'm all yours.

02:23.327 --> 02:24.810
 <i> QUAGMIRE: Little did I know.</i>

02:24.961 --> 02:27.053
      <i> I'll never forget</i>
      <i> that fateful day.</i>

02:27.206 --> 02:29.055
         <i> Looking back,</i>
      <i> I never should have</i>

02:29.150 --> 02:30.724
   <i> tried to do two fantasy</i>
       <i> football drafts</i>

02:30.818 --> 02:32.209
    <i> while flying a plane.</i>

02:32.227 --> 02:35.821
<i>-I ended up with four defenses.</i>
             -Ugh!

02:35.972 --> 02:37.214
   <i> AIR TRAFFIC CONTROLLER:</i>
           <i> FE-117,</i>

02:37.232 --> 02:38.882
          <i> looks like</i>
    <i> you got rough weather.</i>

02:38.884 --> 02:40.325
    <i> Maybe you should just</i>
        <i> do auto-draft</i>

02:40.552 --> 02:42.052
<i>for your fantasy leagues, over.</i>

02:42.070 --> 02:43.737
Uh, negative, negative, Control.

02:43.889 --> 02:45.480
    I am heterosexual, over.

02:45.574 --> 02:47.908
 <i> AIR TRAFFIC CONTROLLER: Ha.</i>
<i> There's that clean-shaven guy</i>

02:48.060 --> 02:49.334
   <i> who cannot spear a fish</i>
        <i> with a stick</i>

02:49.411 --> 02:51.295
  <i> that we all know and love.</i>

02:52.047 --> 02:53.154
           Damn it.

02:53.248 --> 02:55.399
   Too bad I'm in an airplane
         and can only go

02:55.417 --> 02:58.084
     straight into a storm
    and not over or around.

02:58.179 --> 03:00.345
    Wait, I think the storm
        is breaking up.

03:00.572 --> 03:02.906
<i> I was gonna make it, but then</i>

03:02.999 --> 03:05.091
      <i> the plane got hit</i>
        <i> by lightning.</i>

03:05.244 --> 03:06.018
              Oh!

03:06.169 --> 03:07.502
<i>And I somehow drafted the punter</i>

03:07.596 --> 03:09.504
         <i> Jeff Feagles</i>
     <i> in the second round.</i>

03:09.523 --> 03:10.672
              Oh!

03:10.691 --> 03:13.108
     <i> And it was all over.</i>

03:17.198 --> 03:20.532
       <i> I was all alone</i>
   <i> on an uncharted island.</i>

03:20.684 --> 03:21.758
       <i> What could I do?</i>

03:21.777 --> 03:23.109
 <i> Definitely not spear a fish</i>

03:23.262 --> 03:24.761
 <i> with a hand-sharpened stick.</i>

03:24.780 --> 03:26.872
  <i> 'Cause remember, that was a</i>
 <i> complete non-starter for me.</i>

03:27.041 --> 03:29.190
 <i> If I wanted to make it back</i>
        <i> to my Helen,</i>

03:29.284 --> 03:31.268
    <i> I'd need to find a way</i>
          <i> to survive.</i>

03:31.286 --> 03:34.046
     <i> Luckily I had a whole</i>
<i> plane's worth of FedEx parcels</i>

03:34.197 --> 03:35.363
    <i> I could open and use.</i>

03:35.457 --> 03:37.365
      <i> Oh, please be food.</i>
        <i> Please be food.</i>

03:37.384 --> 03:40.219
   Oh, thank God, I'm saved.
        Peanut brittle.

03:40.370 --> 03:41.053
              Aah!

03:41.204 --> 03:43.113
     "From Peter Griffin."

03:43.131 --> 03:45.782
            <i> PETER:</i>
  <i> (laughs) Gotcha. Continue.</i>

03:45.875 --> 03:49.210
           <i> QUAGMIRE:</i>
  <i> But then I opened the most</i>
   <i> important package of all.</i>

03:49.230 --> 03:50.971
<i> My only friend on the island.</i>

03:51.123 --> 03:54.382
   I'm gonna call you Wilson,
       after Rita Wilson,

03:54.401 --> 03:56.960
the most beautiful and talented
      woman in Hollywood.

03:56.979 --> 03:59.571
       The true first lady
      of American culture.

03:59.798 --> 04:02.466
     <i> I swear, I didn't say</i>
<i>all that stuff just so Tom Hanks</i>

04:02.484 --> 04:03.659
 <i> would let us do this movie.</i>

04:06.805 --> 04:08.638
           (grunts)

04:08.657 --> 04:09.806
     Character development.

04:09.825 --> 04:11.157
  <i> I had been on that island</i>

04:11.310 --> 04:12.325
       <i> for four years.</i>

04:12.419 --> 04:14.068
 Man, I've been on this island

04:14.088 --> 04:16.237
     for somewhere between
     two and seven years.

04:16.257 --> 04:18.924
 I'm not sure which 'cause I'm
 no longer obsessed with time.

04:19.075 --> 04:20.150
    <i> That's more character</i>
        <i> development.</i>

04:20.168 --> 04:22.210
<i> Anyway, all these years later,</i>

04:22.321 --> 04:24.838
     <i> I still couldn't get</i>
  <i> Helen Hunt out of my mind.</i>

04:24.990 --> 04:26.673
       <i> I was going nuts</i>
      <i> thinking about her.</i>

04:26.825 --> 04:28.341
          Oh, Helen...

04:28.510 --> 04:30.994
  Oh come on, get it together.
    Think of something else.

04:31.087 --> 04:33.847
   Think of anything besides
          Helen Hunt.

04:33.999 --> 04:35.832
     Oh, almost Helen Hunt.

04:35.851 --> 04:37.276
      <i> Enough was enough.</i>

04:37.427 --> 04:40.279
  <i> I decided to build a raft</i>
 <i> and get back to my beloved.</i>

04:40.430 --> 04:41.947
       <i> But what to make</i>
       <i> the raft out of?</i>

04:42.098 --> 04:43.857
       Got to be something
           I can use.

04:44.009 --> 04:45.951
          What floats?
          What floats?

04:46.178 --> 04:48.662
    Mm, definitely not these
    footballs for Tom Brady.

04:49.865 --> 04:51.373
    Straight to the bottom.

04:57.689 --> 04:59.447
           I wonder.

04:59.525 --> 05:00.690
              Aah!

05:00.709 --> 05:03.376
           <i> PETER:</i>
<i>(laughs) Two for two. Continue.</i>

05:03.470 --> 05:05.028
           <i> QUAGMIRE:</i>
   <i> I was able to float away</i>

05:05.121 --> 05:07.697
        <i> on a raft made</i>
  <i> out of the giant joke box.</i>

05:07.791 --> 05:10.976
   <i> It was me and Wilson and</i>
<i>this one other kind of lame guy.</i>

05:11.127 --> 05:12.311
     Boy, you hoist a sail,

05:12.538 --> 05:14.813
  then where did the wind go?
          Am I right?

05:14.964 --> 05:16.648
        I just saw you
   take a dump in the ocean.

05:16.800 --> 05:18.650
         I'm not really
        looking to chat.

05:19.987 --> 05:21.227
         <i> Days passed.</i>

05:21.380 --> 05:22.988
 <i> Wilson and I were all alone.</i>

05:23.215 --> 05:27.141
       <i> No drinking water</i>
    <i> and no food, except...</i>

05:27.161 --> 05:28.643
      Nope, not this time.

05:28.662 --> 05:30.387
            <i> PETER:</i>
 <i> Eh, you're no fun. Continue.</i>

05:30.389 --> 05:32.998
          <i> QUAGMIRE:</i>
  <i> But then disaster struck.</i>

05:42.067 --> 05:43.991
           Aah! Aah!

05:44.127 --> 05:46.636
        No. No! Wilson!

05:47.997 --> 05:49.255
    <i> Eventually I moved on</i>

05:49.408 --> 05:52.425
<i>and largely forgot about Wilson.</i>

05:52.519 --> 05:54.728
        (piano playing)

06:11.096 --> 06:12.353
  Why are you smiling, honey?

06:12.373 --> 06:14.664
       Oh, I used to bone
        that volleyball.

06:18.027 --> 06:19.452
    <i> I don't remember much</i>
         <i> after that.</i>

06:19.621 --> 06:22.881
  <i> Apparently I was picked up</i>
      <i> by some cargo ship.</i>

06:23.108 --> 06:24.216
          <i> But then,</i>
    <i> wouldn't you know it,</i>

06:24.367 --> 06:27.034
   <i> the ship got taken over</i>
     <i> by Somali pirates.</i>

06:27.054 --> 06:29.054
          Look at me.
          Look at me.

06:29.281 --> 06:31.539
  We are doing this movie now.

06:31.633 --> 06:33.967
          <i> QUAGMIRE:</i>
   <i> Then that Somali pirate</i>
    <i> did a bunch of stuff</i>

06:34.119 --> 06:35.209
    <i> and then nothing else</i>
         <i> ever again,</i>

06:35.303 --> 06:37.120
<i>and eventually I got back home.</i>

06:37.213 --> 06:39.122
 <i> After years and years away,</i>

06:39.141 --> 06:42.067
      <i> it was finally time</i>
       <i> to see my Helen.</i>

06:42.218 --> 06:43.960
   Oh, my God, you're alive.

06:43.979 --> 06:46.053
       I thought about you
        every day, Helen.

06:46.148 --> 06:48.298
You're the reason I stayed alive
        all these years.

06:48.391 --> 06:50.575
  I never stopped loving you.

06:50.727 --> 06:52.560
         I'm-I'm sorry.

06:52.579 --> 06:54.746
       I got back together
        with Paul Reiser.

06:54.973 --> 06:55.914
             What?

06:56.065 --> 06:57.140
 We did a<i> Mad About You</i> reboot

06:57.233 --> 06:58.491
     on Spectrum Originals.

06:58.585 --> 06:59.901
          <i> QUAGMIRE:</i>
   <i> Which just sounds fake.</i>

06:59.995 --> 07:01.235
    <i> I mean, did you watch</i>
        <i> any of that?</i>

07:01.255 --> 07:02.921
<i> Do you even know anyone who...</i>

07:03.072 --> 07:05.924
   <i> I-I... Like, I literally</i>
    <i> do not know one person</i>

07:06.075 --> 07:07.834
        <i> who saw, like,</i>
   <i> a single minute of that.</i>

07:07.928 --> 07:09.243
         I'm so sorry.

07:09.263 --> 07:11.838
          <i> QUAGMIRE:</i>
      <i> I was devastated.</i>

07:11.990 --> 07:14.007
<i> Helen was my first true love--</i>

07:14.101 --> 07:16.083
<i> the only woman I ever wanted--</i>

07:16.103 --> 07:18.103
     <i> and she had moved on</i>
          <i> without me.</i>

07:18.330 --> 07:20.439
<i> Fortunately, five years later,</i>
         <i> they invented</i>

07:20.590 --> 07:22.441
     <i> portable pornography</i>
        <i> on telephones,</i>

07:22.592 --> 07:24.401
   <i> and I've literally never</i>
   <i> thought about her since.</i>

07:32.194 --> 07:36.196
 Well, that was a touching tale
    of first love, Quagmire.

07:36.348 --> 07:39.015
     And I googled Spectrum
     Originals, by the way.

07:39.108 --> 07:42.109
         Found nothing.
          Zero matches.

07:42.129 --> 07:44.111
 Nothing on Ask Jeeves either,

07:44.189 --> 07:46.948
     but they don't always
       have everything.

07:46.967 --> 07:48.967
       Anyway, I remember
         my first love.

07:49.118 --> 07:51.695
It's quite an interesting story.

07:51.713 --> 07:53.955
          Okay, guess
  I'll be going last tonight.

07:54.032 --> 07:57.200
          This was back
       in the early '60s.

07:57.293 --> 07:59.552
        <i> I was working</i>
    <i> at a hoity-toity camp</i>

07:59.646 --> 08:00.870
   <i> for rich Jewish people.</i>

08:00.964 --> 08:02.055
           <i> PETER:</i>
   <i> Are you Jewish in this?</i>

08:02.149 --> 08:04.057
             <i> JOE:</i>
         <i> (laughs) No.</i>

08:04.151 --> 08:06.318
  <i> -I was a dance instructor.</i>
              -♪ ♪

08:06.469 --> 08:08.228
       <i> Anyway, this camp</i>
      <i> was highly renowned</i>

08:08.380 --> 08:11.397
   <i> for offering exclusively</i>
        <i> clean dancing.</i>

08:11.492 --> 08:14.234
  You are the cleanest dancer
          I ever met.

08:14.386 --> 08:16.386
     It's why we come here
          every year.

08:16.479 --> 08:18.479
             <i> JOE:</i>
      <i> But all the while,</i>
      <i> I was being watched</i>

08:18.573 --> 08:21.482
    <i> by the prettiest girl</i>
        <i> in the camp.</i>

08:21.576 --> 08:25.395
<i> Her name was Jennifer Schnozz,</i>
   <i> and I saw her everywhere.</i>

08:25.413 --> 08:28.898
   <i> Seems like she was always</i>
  <i> sniffing around someplace.</i>

08:28.917 --> 08:30.400
          <i> QUAGMIRE:</i>
            <i> Okay.</i>

08:30.493 --> 08:33.236
             <i> JOE:</i>
    <i> Daytimes were reserved</i>
      <i> for clean dancing,</i>

08:33.405 --> 08:35.013
         <i> but at night,</i>
      <i> someone would bring</i>

08:35.240 --> 08:37.832
   <i> a very large watermelon</i>
     <i> to the staff cabin,</i>

08:37.909 --> 08:39.000
     <i> and for some reason,</i>
          <i> that meant</i>

08:39.094 --> 08:41.578
<i> it was time for dirty dancing.</i>

08:41.596 --> 08:43.504
           (cheering)

08:43.598 --> 08:45.673
              ♪ ♪

08:45.767 --> 08:47.842
            <i> JOE:</i>
  <i> We had booze, sexy music,</i>

08:47.936 --> 08:49.861
  <i> and because it was August</i>
         <i> by a lake,</i>

08:50.030 --> 08:51.679
      <i> lots of mosquitos.</i>

08:51.698 --> 08:53.698
           (buzzing)

08:57.279 --> 08:59.854
      <i> My favorite partner</i>
       <i> was Dancy McGee.</i>

08:59.873 --> 09:02.040
   <i> She was the best dancer</i>
        <i> on the staff,</i>

09:02.191 --> 09:04.042
       <i> as you can tell</i>
    <i> from this dance party</i>

09:04.193 --> 09:06.861
      <i> where she's dancing</i>
   <i> neither better nor worse</i>

09:06.955 --> 09:09.530
  <i> than anyone on the staff.</i>

09:09.699 --> 09:12.108
<i> But there Jennifer was again,</i>

09:12.127 --> 09:14.535
     <i> always with her nose</i>
  <i> pressed against the glass,</i>

09:14.629 --> 09:17.630
   <i> or anything else she was</i>
<i> standing three feet away from.</i>

09:17.783 --> 09:19.707
          <i> QUAGMIRE:</i>
  <i> Might be going a bit hard</i>
    <i> with the nose stuff.</i>

09:19.726 --> 09:22.285
             <i> JOE:</i>
      <i> Relax, she's fine.</i>
      <i> She got a new one.</i>

09:22.304 --> 09:24.545
 <i> It was time to make my move.</i>

09:24.565 --> 09:25.880
       Hey, do I know you?

09:25.899 --> 09:27.473
              Yeah.
    We were both in<i> Red Dawn</i>

09:27.568 --> 09:30.885
 and we probably had sex on set
     and then you dumped me

09:30.904 --> 09:32.553
       and now we famously
        hate each other.

09:32.647 --> 09:34.239
       Oh, yeah, Jennifer.

09:34.390 --> 09:37.909
          Well, welcome
       to the Poke-a-nose.

09:38.136 --> 09:39.894
   <i> That was kind of my joke</i>
         <i> around camp.</i>

09:39.988 --> 09:41.154
       <i> People loved it,</i>
      <i> way better than my</i>

09:41.306 --> 09:43.230
<i>"welcome to the Catskills" bit.</i>

09:43.250 --> 09:46.233
    <i> I was not invited back</i>
         <i> to that camp.</i>

09:46.253 --> 09:48.569
        Joe, come quick!
           It's Dancy.

09:48.738 --> 09:50.571
       What's the matter?

09:50.665 --> 09:52.482
       It's-it's my jaw.

09:52.651 --> 09:53.817
       It's very clicky.

09:53.910 --> 09:55.927
  I th... I think I have TMJ.

09:56.154 --> 09:57.912
             -TMJ?
           -Oh, no!

09:57.989 --> 09:59.339
       I hear that causes
         mild discomfort

09:59.491 --> 10:01.341
     but doesn't otherwise
   interfere with lifestyle.

10:01.493 --> 10:02.934
            <i> JOE:</i>
    <i> Of course, back then,</i>
       <i> it was illegal</i>

10:03.161 --> 10:04.344
      <i> to get jaw surgery.</i>

10:04.496 --> 10:06.329
        <i> The only places</i>
       <i> that would do it</i>

10:06.348 --> 10:09.015
    <i> were sketchy, unsafe,</i>
   <i> back-alley jaw clinics.</i>

10:09.167 --> 10:11.501
       Do you want to keep
            the TMJ?

10:11.519 --> 10:14.946
         Come on, Joe.
     I'm single, I'm poor,

10:15.098 --> 10:16.522
    I work at a Jewish camp
           for tips.

10:16.691 --> 10:17.949
            <i> PETER:</i>
         <i> Ugh. Brutal.</i>

10:18.026 --> 10:20.510
